# armour/shared/pauldron_flame2_r: the small FLAME pauldron on the right shoulder (flame.2; ARMOUR-X, wave 2: PLAN "The envelope in production", STYLE_P2 29).
# tongues of flame licking up off a banded cop (the legend drawing one column and one row smaller): the tallest
# tongue 4 px over the cop curling outward, a smaller one beside it; a rim and a lame under the band.
# 1 px past the 16 px shoulder line facing D (18 across with its pair; STYLE_P2 29.3).
# Rides the lean and the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`).
# Finish regions: R the rims, G the tongues' hearts, N the seam under the band, P the tongues and the band.
# Shared by the man and the woman (D10). Generated by ARMOUR-X genx.py from shapesx.py (re-run, never
# hand-edit the derived views). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
